A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Wheat and the Weeds, the Hidden Treasure and the Pearl, and the Mustard Seed and the Leaven are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. This parable makes no use of their meanings, and they make none of this one.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus compares the kingdom of heaven to a net cast into the sea that gathered of every kind, was drawn to shore when full, and was sorted, the good gathered into vessels and the bad cast away. He says that so it shall be at the end of the world: the angels shall sever the wicked from among the just and cast them into the furnace of fire, where there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth. He names nothing else in the story. He then says that every scribe instructed unto the kingdom of heaven is like a householder who brings forth out of his treasure things new and old, and He gives no explanation.'))
A(('p', 'Write the synthesis in your own words in five to seven sentences. In it:'))
