A(('call', 'Boundaries to Remember',
   'Jesus names the end of the world, the angels, the wicked, the just, the furnace of fire and the wailing and gnashing of teeth, and nothing more. No identity for the net, the sea, the vessels, the fishermen, the householder or the treasure. No symbol carried in from another parable. Gathering, sorting and bringing forth are actions in a story and a saying, not steps of salvation. The Body of Christ is neither the net nor the vessels. The lessons are principles of conduct, not a transfer of Kingdom identity to the Body.'))
